Open-core boundary
------------------
Tugra follows an open-core model. This repository is the Community edition: the
full self-hosted product, licensed under the GNU AGPL-3.0 (see LICENSE); the
agent and CLI are MIT (see agent/LICENSE). Contributions are accepted under a
CLA (see CLA.md) so the core can be dual-licensed.

The Pro and Cloud editions are a proprietary layer built on top of this core.
Their source is NOT part of this repository or the OSS Docker image — it lives in
separate, private packages (the reserved "@tugra/cloud-*" namespace; see
proprietary/README.md). The edition-gating primitive shipped here (requireEdition)
carries no proprietary code; it only marks where such features would attach.
Editions and the feature matrix are documented in docs/open-core.md. A commercial
license is available at license@tugra.io.

This product includes third-party material:

One-click service templates
---------------------------
The bulk service catalog in apps/hub-api/src/templates/catalog.generated.json
is adapted (transformed) from Coolify's service templates.
  Source:  https://github.com/coollabsio/coolify (templates/service-templates.json)
  License: Apache License 2.0
Templates are programmatically converted to Tugra's compose + secret model by
scripts/import-templates.mjs; the original compose definitions remain under the
Apache-2.0 license of their respective upstream project.

